# Prettier formats the code: Apex, JavaScript, CSS and the workflow YAML.
# Metadata XML is left as Salesforce writes it: the XML formatter breaks long
# descriptions across two lines in an odd way, and the hard-rule checks read
# those descriptions. These stay as they are too:

# Component templates. Prettier moves text onto its own line next to a tag,
# which is harmless on a web page, but the LWC compiler drops whitespace that
# contains a line break, so "Updated <time>" renders as "Updatedtime".
**/lwc/**/*.html

# Built by `npm run guide` from guide/pages; the build check compares them
# byte for byte with what the generator writes.
force-app/main/default/lwc/guidePage*/
force-app/main/default/lwc/guideContent/
force-app/main/default/lwc/guideCatalog/

# The Grid Guide's page sources and files, hand-written and tested word for word.
guide/pages/
guide/files/

# Prose, data and binary-like assets.
*.md
*.json
*.csv
docs/
**/staticresources/
**/contentassets/

# Tooling output.
node_modules/
coverage/
.sfdx/
.sf/
.husky/_/
